  "limitations": [
    "Only the no_revert_mint_succeeds impact is formalized; the minted Q96 amount, multiplier, and insolvency impacts are handled in separate passes.",
    "The Q96 cap alternative in the intent is not separately encoded; the market-supply bound is used as the applicability condition.",
    "The Q96 cap and the market supply are treated as the same token-denominated bound; the report's 'or the Q96 cap' alternative is not separately encoded because the selected scenario has mint_amount == Q96 and supply 1,000.",
    "The relation encodes the desired outcome as zero tokens minted when the mint amount exceeds the market supply; the report's actual impact is that Q96 tokens are minted.",
    "The Q96 cap and market supply bound are formalized as a single bounded_value relation on mint_amount vs market_base_token_supply; the report's OR-of-two-conditions cap structure is not separately modeled.",
    "Insolvency is represented as a boolean unbacked-token outcome rather than a numeric reserve deficit because no reserve quantity is reported.",
